  "meta": {
    "today": "2026-09-07",
    "weekday": "Monday",
    "version": "time-2.0",
    "note": "Expanded probe, 24 single-action tasks. Built to test F19: the two large models solved «половина X» and failed every «N минут X-ого», which suggests scale buys coverage of frequent fixed phrases and not the productive rule. So the counting-into-the-hour category is split by how fixed the phrase is: half_past (most frequent), quarter_past (intermediate), n_minutes (fully productive, varying both the minute count and the hour). Prediction: large models hold half_past, degrade on quarter_past, fail n_minutes; small models fail all three. literal and subtractive are unchanged controls. subtractive additionally rules out the rival explanation that this is the known LLM +-1 temporal bias (Khodja et al. 2025, Fatemi et al. 2025): a general +-1 bias would appear in English too, and English is parallel at every clock time here."
  },
